The requirement registers a traveler account. Existing entities: session, user_account. Need to decide reuse. The registration creates an account and a session. So write to user_account and session, read user_account (for uniqueness check - username and email uniqueness). Read user_account to check duplicates.

Do we need a new entity for traveler profile? The account stores name, passport, nationality, gender, DOB, email, password, username. These are attributes of user_account. Could introduce a new entity "traveler" but user_account already represents registered visitor account. The description says "A registered visitor account whose saved username is shown in the header after registration or login." That fits. So reuse user_account.

Read: user_account (uniqueness checks). Write: user_account, session.

So reuse_entities: ["user_account", "session"], new_entities: [].

read: ["user_account"], write: ["user_account", "session"].

